# Collisional ionization / recombination of hydrogen (PRIZMO format).
# One-zone test: reaches collisional-ionization equilibrium (CIE).
#   k_ion*n_H*n_e = k_rec*n_Hp*n_e  ->  x/(1-x) = k_ion(Tgas)/k_rec(Tgas)
# n_e cancels, so equilibrium ionization fraction is a pure function of Tgas.
# NOTE: set Tgas ~ 1e4-1e5 K, else exp(-157809/Tgas) ~ 0 and nothing ionizes.
# Rates from Cen (1992), ApJS 78, 341, Table 1.

# collisional ionization (Cen 1992)
H + E -> H+ + E + E   []   5.85e-11*sqrt(Tgas)*exp(-157809.1/Tgas)/(1+sqrt(Tgas/1e5))

# radiative recombination, case A (Cen 1992)
H+ + E -> H           []   8.40e-11/sqrt(Tgas)*(Tgas/1e3)**(-0.2)/(1+(Tgas/1e6)**0.7)
